WEBVTT

00:00:00.010 --> 00:00:01.829
Welcome to Resgrid Academy.

00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:06.320
In this lesson, we will keep incident and prevention records reviewable.

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:10.960
Incident information becomes harder to review and report when it is spread across

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:14.140
calls, attachments, and separate files.

00:00:14.309 --> 00:00:18.039
We will explain the features, the setup decisions, and a

00:00:18.039 --> 00:00:20.129
practical way to check the result.

00:00:20.969 --> 00:00:24.939
After each call, the officer completes an incident report from the

00:00:24.939 --> 00:00:27.079
call and a supervisor reviews it.

00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:30.990
Keep incident and activity records with the calls they came from,

00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:32.910
ready for review and reporting.

00:00:33.070 --> 00:00:37.040
The examples in this series use a fictional department and are teaching

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:39.419
scenarios, not default settings.

00:00:40.312 --> 00:00:40.902
Logs.

00:00:41.112 --> 00:00:44.032
Activity logs for calls, training and work.

00:00:44.272 --> 00:00:46.542
Choose the log types members complete.

00:00:46.752 --> 00:00:49.282
Availability also depends on Logs.

00:00:49.501 --> 00:00:51.732
Check access in the target department.

00:00:52.512 --> 00:00:53.302
Records.

00:00:53.501 --> 00:00:55.632
Incident and activity records.

00:00:55.861 --> 00:00:59.832
Turn on Records if it is available to you and review the record settings.

00:01:00.052 --> 00:01:02.581
Availability also depends on Logs.

00:01:02.802 --> 00:01:05.041
Check access in the target department.

00:01:05.812 --> 00:01:07.081
Incident reports.

00:01:07.282 --> 00:01:09.391
Incident reports linked to calls.

00:01:09.601 --> 00:01:12.511
Decide who completes and who reviews each report.

00:01:13.271 --> 00:01:15.211
Record definitions and templates.

00:01:15.581 --> 00:01:17.781
The forms and fields records use.

00:01:18.011 --> 00:01:21.361
Start from the built-in forms and add only the fields you need.

00:01:22.151 --> 00:01:22.911
Reports.

00:01:23.111 --> 00:01:26.721
Department reports on calls, personnel and activity.

00:01:26.881 --> 00:01:29.822
Run the reports you use for meetings or compliance.

00:01:30.041 --> 00:01:32.561
Availability also depends on Reports.

00:01:32.931 --> 00:01:35.171
Check access in the target department.

00:01:35.951 --> 00:01:36.552
New Log.

00:01:36.732 --> 00:01:39.921
Record a run report, training log or work log.

00:01:40.111 --> 00:01:43.692
Know which reports your department completes and who reviews them.

00:01:43.881 --> 00:01:46.861
Records may need to be enabled for your department.

00:01:47.041 --> 00:01:49.571
Availability also depends on Logs.

00:01:49.791 --> 00:01:52.031
Check access in the target department.

00:01:52.812 --> 00:01:54.172
Records Dashboard.

00:01:54.331 --> 00:01:57.952
Records that are due, awaiting review or ready to submit.

00:01:58.101 --> 00:02:01.692
Know which reports your department completes and who reviews them.

00:02:01.871 --> 00:02:04.841
Records may need to be enabled for your department.

00:02:05.022 --> 00:02:07.562
Availability also depends on Logs.

00:02:07.741 --> 00:02:09.981
Check access in the target department.

00:02:10.751 --> 00:02:11.872
Records Settings.

00:02:12.081 --> 00:02:16.451
Numbering, retention, search and visibility rules for records.

00:02:16.651 --> 00:02:20.241
Know which reports your department completes and who reviews them.

00:02:20.421 --> 00:02:23.401
Records may need to be enabled for your department.

00:02:23.571 --> 00:02:26.121
Availability also depends on Logs.

00:02:26.291 --> 00:02:28.531
Check access in the target department.

00:02:29.331 --> 00:02:31.142
Occupancies and preplans.

00:02:31.361 --> 00:02:35.311
Buildings and sites with their contacts, hazards and preplans.

00:02:35.522 --> 00:02:39.101
Know which reports your department completes and who reviews them.

00:02:39.281 --> 00:02:42.261
Records may need to be enabled for your department.

00:02:43.041 --> 00:02:43.961
Inspections.

00:02:44.221 --> 00:02:47.652
Schedule inspections and track violations and corrections.

00:02:47.842 --> 00:02:51.421
Know which reports your department completes and who reviews them.

00:02:51.611 --> 00:02:54.591
Records may need to be enabled for your department.

00:02:55.391 --> 00:02:57.081
Hydrants and water sources.

00:02:57.322 --> 00:03:00.932
Hydrants and water sources with their inspection and flow history.

00:03:01.091 --> 00:03:04.671
Know which reports your department completes and who reviews them.

00:03:04.852 --> 00:03:09.102
Records may need to be enabled for your department. Permits.

00:03:09.462 --> 00:03:11.382
Permits and their approval status.

00:03:11.582 --> 00:03:15.152
Know which reports your department completes and who reviews them.

00:03:15.342 --> 00:03:18.322
Records may need to be enabled for your department.

00:03:19.091 --> 00:03:20.271
Investigations.

00:03:20.471 --> 00:03:24.492
Restricted case records, such as fire investigations.

00:03:24.681 --> 00:03:28.272
Know which reports your department completes and who reviews them.

00:03:28.452 --> 00:03:31.432
Records may need to be enabled for your department.

00:03:32.212 --> 00:03:34.191
Evidence capture and provenance.

00:03:34.442 --> 00:03:37.191
Collect and track evidence attached to a record.

00:03:37.382 --> 00:03:40.961
Know which reports your department completes and who reviews them.

00:03:41.142 --> 00:03:44.121
Records may need to be enabled for your department.

00:03:44.901 --> 00:03:45.841
