00:03:46.061 --> 00:03:49.092
Legal holds that stop records from being deleted.

00:03:49.271 --> 00:03:52.841
Know which reports your department completes and who reviews them.

00:03:53.032 --> 00:03:56.011
Records may need to be enabled for your department.

00:03:56.782 --> 00:03:58.162
Reporting submissions.

00:03:58.401 --> 00:04:02.322
Submit incident reports to state or national reporting systems.

00:04:02.541 --> 00:04:06.131
Know which reports your department completes and who reviews them.

00:04:06.302 --> 00:04:09.251
Records may need to be enabled for your department.

00:04:10.072 --> 00:04:11.422
Records analytics.

00:04:11.622 --> 00:04:15.252
Response, workload and readiness trends from your records.

00:04:15.462 --> 00:04:19.031
Know which reports your department completes and who reviews them.

00:04:19.222 --> 00:04:22.201
Records may need to be enabled for your department.

00:04:23.022 --> 00:04:24.571
Saved record reports.

00:04:24.832 --> 00:04:27.232
Saved record reports you can run again.

00:04:27.431 --> 00:04:31.011
Know which reports your department completes and who reviews them.

00:04:31.191 --> 00:04:34.172
Records may need to be enabled for your department.

00:04:34.941 --> 00:04:36.661
Record exports and templates.

00:04:37.031 --> 00:04:39.681
Export records to files using templates.

00:04:40.031 --> 00:04:43.611
Know which reports your department completes and who reviews them.

00:04:43.792 --> 00:04:46.771
Records may need to be enabled for your department.

00:04:47.531 --> 00:04:48.922
Disclosure requests.

00:04:49.301 --> 00:04:53.071
Requests to release records, with redaction and approval.

00:04:53.231 --> 00:04:56.812
Know which reports your department completes and who reviews them.

00:04:56.992 --> 00:04:59.961
Records may need to be enabled for your department.

00:05:00.762 --> 00:05:06.161
Post-finalization review uses rubrics, sampling, scores, and trends

00:05:06.161 --> 00:05:08.441
to identify reporting follow-up.

00:05:08.671 --> 00:05:10.981
Confirm rollout and reviewer access,

00:05:11.191 --> 00:05:13.001
configure an approved rubric,

00:05:13.242 --> 00:05:16.881
sample finalized records, and score a demo review.

00:05:17.032 --> 00:05:23.092
Review criteria, sample scope, notes, and amendment recommendations without treating

00:05:23.092 --> 00:05:25.372
a score as a rewritten incident report.

00:05:25.571 --> 00:05:28.582
Confirm availability in the demo department before

00:05:28.582 --> 00:05:30.241
recording the live workflow.

00:05:31.032 --> 00:05:35.511
Records health and prevention attachment screens make retained record support

00:05:35.511 --> 00:05:37.861
and issues visible to authorized users.

00:05:38.051 --> 00:05:42.022
Review the records health view and attach a synthetic support file to

00:05:42.022 --> 00:05:44.161
an appropriate prevention record.

00:05:44.321 --> 00:05:48.501
Verify parent-record access and the restricted-attachment behavior

00:05:48.501 --> 00:05:50.361
on the intended member account.

00:05:50.571 --> 00:05:53.571
Confirm availability in the demo department before

00:05:53.571 --> 00:05:55.231
recording the live workflow.

00:05:56.021 --> 00:06:00.011
Incident analysis is a separately validated and submitted artifact

00:06:00.011 --> 00:06:01.801
linked to an incident report.

00:06:02.011 --> 00:06:04.441
Start analysis from a demo incident,

00:06:04.591 --> 00:06:08.992
edit and validate it, then review finalization and submission readiness.

00:06:09.191 --> 00:06:13.412
Confirm the analysis lifecycle separately from the incident report.

00:06:13.611 --> 00:06:17.542
Submission waits for the required incident destination identity.

00:06:17.742 --> 00:06:20.741
Confirm availability in the demo department before

00:06:20.741 --> 00:06:22.402
recording the live workflow.

00:06:23.211 --> 00:06:26.661
Community risk reduction records education and prevention

00:06:26.661 --> 00:06:28.462
activity with attendee counts.

00:06:28.851 --> 00:06:31.632
Confirm the community-risk feature and access,

00:06:31.791 --> 00:06:36.351
record a fictional activity, and review its summary and analytics scope.

00:06:36.551 --> 00:06:42.201
Check counts, dates, ownership, and the activity audience without placing attendee

00:06:42.201 --> 00:06:44.602
personal information into the example.

00:06:44.791 --> 00:06:47.801
Confirm availability in the demo department before

00:06:47.801 --> 00:06:49.451
recording the live workflow.

00:06:50.264 --> 00:06:54.634
Revision and difference views help reviewers understand how a record changed.

00:06:54.834 --> 00:06:58.654
Open two revisions of a synthetic record and review their differences

00:06:58.654 --> 00:07:00.284
and any permitted export.

00:07:00.444 --> 00:07:03.994
Confirm the selected revisions and access to the parent record

00:07:03.994 --> 00:07:05.964
before interpreting the difference.

00:07:06.204 --> 00:07:09.204
Confirm availability in the demo department before

00:07:09.204 --> 00:07:10.873
recording the live workflow.

00:07:11.723 --> 00:07:15.953
Submission details and reconciliation keep a recorded report distinct

00:07:15.963 --> 00:07:18.194
from its external filing outcome.

00:07:18.373 --> 00:07:22.423
Review a test submission status and reconcile a known destination

00:07:22.423 --> 00:07:24.414
response through the owning workflow.

00:07:24.594 --> 00:07:28.613
Check the destination identity, accepted or failed outcome,

00:07:28.774 --> 00:07:30.314
and any corrections needed.

00:07:30.533 --> 00:07:33.543
Confirm availability in the demo department before

00:07:33.544 --> 00:07:35.203
recording the live workflow.

00:07:36.004 --> 00:07:39.773
Record inventory workflows connect consumption and evidence to the

00:07:39.774 --> 00:07:41.773
incident or activity record.

00:07:41.943 --> 00:07:46.544
Link synthetic inventory use to a record, refresh its evidence, and

00:07:46.544 --> 00:07:48.743
review supported reversal handling.

00:07:48.903 --> 00:07:54.183
Reconcile the record, item, quantity, and corresponding stock movement.

00:07:54.393 --> 00:07:57.393
Confirm availability in the demo department before

00:07:57.393 --> 00:07:59.054
recording the live workflow.

00:07:59.834 --> 00:08:03.574
Deployment connector screens manage connector configuration,

00:08:03.743 --> 00:08:06.343
enablement, tokens, and runs.

00:08:06.533 --> 00:08:11.073
Review connector terms and ownership, configure a demo destination,

00:08:11.233 --> 00:08:13.073
and inspect a controlled run.

00:08:13.263 --> 00:08:18.023
Confirm the target integration, observed run, and token lifecycle.

00:08:18.184 --> 00:08:20.343
Mask credentials during capture.

00:08:20.563 --> 00:08:23.563
Confirm availability in the demo department before

00:08:23.563 --> 00:08:25.224
recording the live workflow.

00:08:26.044 --> 00:08:28.964
For the training scenario, work in this order.

00:08:29.163 --> 00:08:33.653
Step 1. Review record settings, definitions, numbering,

00:08:33.824 --> 00:08:35.824
visibility, and retention.

00:08:36.044 --> 00:08:39.443
Step 2. Create a report linked to a training call and

00:08:39.523 --> 00:08:41.313
complete its required data.

00:08:41.523 --> 00:08:46.884
Step 3. Use review, evidence, exports, or submission workflows

00:08:46.884 --> 00:08:48.373
appropriate to the record.

00:08:49.163 --> 00:08:50.803
Now verify the result.

00:08:51.033 --> 00:08:56.453
Check draft and review status, evidence provenance, restricted access, and the

00:08:56.453 --> 00:08:58.813
actual outcome of any test submission.

00:08:59.024 --> 00:09:02.683
A common problem to watch for: A queued submission is not

00:09:02.683 --> 00:09:04.673
acceptance by its destination.

00:09:04.843 --> 00:09:08.733
Legal holds and disclosure reviews require their owning workflows.

00:09:09.533 --> 00:09:11.393
Your practice task is simple.

00:09:11.563 --> 00:09:15.913
Prepare one complete training incident report and one incomplete draft.

00:09:16.063 --> 00:09:20.023
Use the work queue to assign corrections and compare analytics scope.

00:09:20.233 --> 00:09:24.724
Record the result, who owns the follow-up, and when it should be reviewed.

